<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Slavonia</h1><p class="st-meta">1699 CE – 1868 CE · capital Osijek</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Habsburg crown land between the Drava and Sava rivers, reconquered from the Ottomans in 1699 and rebuilt with new settlers and baroque towns.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> armies drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> in 1699 confirmed the conquest. The reclaimed land was divided between a civilian part, organised as the counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pozega-croatia">Požega</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virovitica">Virovitica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Srijem</a>, and a southern strip along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> placed in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/military-frontier">Military Frontier</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> was depopulated by war, so the crown and new landowners brought in German, Hungarian, Slovak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serb</a> settlers. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osijek">Osijek's</a> fortress, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrda">Tvrđa</a>, was rebuilt in the 1710s and 1720s, and the bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakovo">Đakovo</a> revived Catholic life, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Serbs were organised around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sremski-karlovci">Sremski Karlovci</a>. From 1745 the civil counties were placed under the Croatian ban and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-parliament">Sabor</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> remained formally a separate kingdom within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lands-of-the-crown-of-saint-stephen">Lands of the Hungarian Crown</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-hungarian-settlement">Croatian-Hungarian Settlement</a> of 1868 joined it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-croatia-slavonia">Kingdom of Croatia-Slavonia</a>. The eastern part, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Srijem</a>, was divided between Croatia and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> after 1945.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-slavonia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Slavonia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Havsjö · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colours_of_Slavonia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1699 CE – 1868 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Osijek</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic and Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Croatian, German, Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Habsburg Slavonia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1784&amp;focus=kingdom-of-slavonia" aria-label="Kingdom of Slavonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5123 571 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Slavonia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5443 827L5709 970M5443 827L5381 747M5443 827L5381 747M5443 827L5378 819"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5381 747h0M5381 747h0M5378 819h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5443 827h0"/><path class="map